WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:05.070 --> 00:05.700
Eureka!

00:08.930 --> 00:10.180
How long are you intending to sleep?

00:11.860 --> 00:13.080
Wake up, Eureka.

00:14.970 --> 00:15.890
Bro...

00:16.440 --> 00:17.680
What's with the outfit...?

00:18.000 --> 00:18.850
What do you mean, "what"?

00:19.330 --> 00:21.040
I am getting married today!

00:21.790 --> 00:22.210
Ma-

00:22.760 --> 00:23.410
Married?!

00:23.710 --> 00:24.170
That is right.

00:24.900 --> 00:27.180
I am going to leave the Miare Gym to you.

00:27.740 --> 00:28.500
Take good care of it.

00:28.980 --> 00:29.810
What?!

00:30.340 --> 00:31.890
Hey, wait a second, bro!

00:32.260 --> 00:33.700
Come on, hurry up and get dressed.

00:34.930 --> 00:36.730
Make sure to come in a really nice outfit.

00:38.620 --> 00:39.950
What?!

00:50.670 --> 00:53.840
Wha- Are you really getting married, bro?

00:54.110 --> 00:55.520
Bro!

00:57.520 --> 01:00.700
Bro!

01:05.660 --> 01:07.780
There's no way my bro would...

01:07.780 --> 01:09.740
Nope, nope. Never.

01:21.220 --> 01:26.930
A Bride for Citron!?
Eureka's S’il-vous-plalt Panic!!

01:27.900 --> 01:37.750
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:27.900 --> 01:37.750
Z

01:27.990 --> 01:31.670
Aiming to enter the Kalos League,

01:32.010 --> 01:33.890
Satoshi and his friends continue their journey in order to get the eighth badge.

01:34.570 --> 01:35.810
A weird dream?

01:35.810 --> 01:38.140
Yeah, a really weird one.

01:38.140 --> 01:38.740
What kind?

01:40.040 --> 01:40.930
Uh...

01:41.560 --> 01:42.130
It's a secret.

01:42.590 --> 01:45.910
Some dreams are precognitive, so you better watch out.

01:46.390 --> 01:47.190
"Precognitive"?

01:47.590 --> 01:50.410
That's right. It means that what you dreamed about actually happens in real life.

01:50.870 --> 01:51.870
What...?

01:51.870 --> 01:52.580
Hey, Citron.

01:53.190 --> 01:54.670
Eat your breakfast.

01:56.270 --> 01:58.130
I will be done in a second.

02:02.170 --> 02:02.670
Cough...

02:03.160 --> 02:04.680
I have done it again.

02:06.780 --> 02:08.380
It can't be! Never!

02:40.850 --> 02:41.560
Horubee!

02:42.630 --> 02:43.240
Did you find it?

02:45.560 --> 02:47.160
Bro, look!

02:47.670 --> 02:48.640
It is a Mimirol!

02:51.880 --> 02:53.650
Mimirol, the Rabbit Pokémon.

02:53.900 --> 03:00.070
When it feels danger, it perks up its ears. On cold nights, it sleeps with its head tucked into the fur on its body.

03:00.570 --> 03:02.320
It's so cute!

03:02.320 --> 03:02.800
Yeah!

03:03.290 --> 03:05.010
Mimirol, where are you?

03:08.220 --> 03:09.470
There you are.

03:09.960 --> 03:11.500
Oh my, is that a friend?

03:12.320 --> 03:12.690
Oh?

03:13.030 --> 03:15.290
Is that Mimirol your Pokémon?

03:15.900 --> 03:18.500
That's right. Does that Horubee belong to you?

03:19.240 --> 03:19.570
Yes.

03:19.960 --> 03:22.250
I want to keep this pretty lady!

03:23.020 --> 03:25.630
Please have my brother, s'il-vous-plaît!

03:28.110 --> 03:30.760
I want you to become my brother's bride!

03:30.760 --> 03:33.950
My bro has nothing but mechanics in his head and he's a bit slow,

03:33.950 --> 03:36.680
so I'd like for him to have a reliable wife...

03:36.680 --> 03:39.470
Eureka, I told you to stop doing that!

03:41.130 --> 03:41.900
Why?!

03:42.620 --> 03:44.070
Oh, how convenient.

03:44.470 --> 03:46.940
The truth is, I'm searching for a partner as well.

03:47.410 --> 03:48.910
I'm Lillia. Nice to meet you.

03:49.470 --> 03:49.680
Huh?

03:51.320 --> 03:52.360
By the way, what's this?

03:53.100 --> 03:54.320
It is an Eipam Arm.

03:54.320 --> 03:55.710
That's a fine device!

03:55.710 --> 03:57.020
I made it!

03:57.020 --> 04:01.160
Amazing! I'm very interested in devices like this one.

04:02.750 --> 04:03.110
Here you go.

04:03.610 --> 04:04.470
Thank you.

04:05.160 --> 04:09.770
Wow! Your father is the president of Orange Logo?

04:10.430 --> 04:11.120
That's right.

04:11.730 --> 04:16.460
Orange Logo is the leading robot manufacturer in the industry, is it not?

04:16.950 --> 04:19.030
Wow, that's amazing!

04:20.390 --> 04:21.740
It is <i>too</i> amazing!

04:21.740 --> 04:22.400
I'd rather talk about your...

04:22.970 --> 04:25.110
...What was it? Eipam Arm?

04:25.640 --> 04:26.820
That one's amazing too!

04:27.310 --> 04:30.200
Citron is good at making all kinds of devices. Aren't you?

04:30.510 --> 04:33.260
You are exaggerating...

04:33.260 --> 04:34.330
I just do it as a hobby...

04:34.860 --> 04:37.020
He's got a robot called the "Citroid" too!

04:38.380 --> 04:39.600
Geez, Satoshi!

04:44.360 --> 04:46.460
They're all really interesting...

04:47.160 --> 04:50.540
This Eipam Arm is connected to my backpack.

04:50.870 --> 04:51.980
Amazing.

04:52.360 --> 04:53.970
What an interesting idea!

04:54.790 --> 04:58.550
We've got out of trouble countless times thanks to Citron!

04:58.550 --> 04:59.020
Yeah.

04:59.640 --> 05:00.560
Wow...!

05:00.950 --> 05:04.510
Lillia-san, you mentioned you were looking for a partner...

05:04.890 --> 05:08.260
I have to succeed my father someday.

05:08.810 --> 05:10.890
Will you become the president, Lillia-san?

05:11.600 --> 05:12.110
No.

05:12.780 --> 05:15.400
Whoever becomes my partner will.

05:16.240 --> 05:17.120
I see.

05:17.820 --> 05:18.400
Good.

05:19.040 --> 05:20.570
What?!

05:21.170 --> 05:23.340
Bro!

05:24.690 --> 05:25.310
Eureka!

05:25.990 --> 05:28.450
Come to think of it, I have not introduced her yet, have I?

05:29.660 --> 05:31.360
This is my bride, Lillia-san.

05:31.760 --> 05:32.560
I'm Lillia.

05:32.890 --> 05:33.760
Nice to meet you.

05:34.120 --> 05:37.900
I have become the president of Lillia-san's company, Orange Logo.

05:38.460 --> 05:41.690
so I am leaving the Miare Gym to you, Eureka.

05:42.170 --> 05:43.830
What?!

05:45.150 --> 05:45.950
Darling,

05:46.330 --> 05:47.560
I've poured you some tea.

05:48.230 --> 05:49.350
Why don't you take a little break?

05:49.810 --> 05:50.320
Thank you.

05:55.030 --> 05:56.590
No way...

05:58.480 --> 05:59.900
What's the matter, Eureka?

05:59.900 --> 06:02.570
Hey, Serena. Pinch my cheek.

06:02.570 --> 06:03.530
Why?

06:03.530 --> 06:04.170
Just do it!

06:07.450 --> 06:08.940
Ow!

06:09.480 --> 06:11.760
It really isn't a dream!

06:13.570 --> 06:14.240
Oh my.

06:14.960 --> 06:16.000
Are you hungry?

06:16.380 --> 06:17.510
Shall I cook something?

06:18.290 --> 06:20.830
Citron's cooking tastes really great!

06:21.200 --> 06:22.970
Then I'll take you up on your offer.

06:23.390 --> 06:25.360
Geez, Satoshi...!

06:29.840 --> 06:32.690
You even use machines to <i>cook</i>? Amazing!

06:33.070 --> 06:35.450
Bro, Eureka's hungry too!

06:35.960 --> 06:38.370
Eureka, you just ate.

06:42.080 --> 06:44.890
Mimirol seems to have taken a liking to Horubee.

07:11.820 --> 07:13.820
Oh, a Mimirol.

07:14.210 --> 07:16.130
That's a cute Pokémon.

07:16.130 --> 07:17.950
If I have that that Mimirol next to me,

07:18.720 --> 07:24.720
I think it'll be able to enhance my beauty, the beauty of an adult brimming with mature sex appeal, even further.

07:25.470 --> 07:26.630
Is that so?

07:27.550 --> 07:28.550
Yes, it is so.

07:28.840 --> 07:31.190
That's how the world works.

07:31.190 --> 07:32.170
I see.

07:32.850 --> 07:34.530
We'll get that Mimirol...

07:35.080 --> 07:36.920
...so it can bring out my beauty.

07:37.330 --> 07:38.180
Right, right.

07:38.920 --> 07:43.480
It's true that that Mimirol might bring some charm to the Rocket Gang.

07:44.150 --> 07:44.960
"Charm"?

07:45.290 --> 07:48.680
The Pokémon we have right now, be it Maaiika or Pumpjin,

07:49.110 --> 07:51.050
lack cuteness.

07:51.050 --> 07:52.860
Maaiika is <i>very</i> cute!

07:53.350 --> 07:55.430
Anyway... The keyword is "charm"!

07:55.840 --> 07:56.400
So it's decided.

07:56.760 --> 07:57.910
We'll get Mimirol.

08:01.170 --> 08:03.130
Whoa, it's delicious!

08:03.130 --> 08:03.920
I know, right?

08:04.290 --> 08:06.460
So you're a good cook too, how wonderful!

08:06.460 --> 08:07.120
It is nothing...

08:11.010 --> 08:12.240
Oh, wait.

08:12.700 --> 08:15.090
I'll add a little Honeymitsu to your tea...

08:16.670 --> 08:17.250
Here you go.

08:21.720 --> 08:22.560
So sweet...

08:24.920 --> 08:26.610
All right, open up.

08:30.680 --> 08:32.000
It is delicious.

08:32.380 --> 08:34.380
And then my bro will say,

08:34.780 --> 08:37.430
"I am the happiest person in the world."

08:37.430 --> 08:37.910
That's what he'll say.

08:49.320 --> 08:50.490
Dedenne!

08:50.490 --> 08:53.360
What have you done?! Apologize!

08:56.510 --> 08:57.470
It's fine.

08:58.620 --> 08:59.990
Dedenne, nice one.

09:04.250 --> 09:04.940
You two,

09:06.150 --> 09:07.430
why don't you go for a walk?

09:13.020 --> 09:14.730
Horubee-kun, I'm counting on you.

09:18.910 --> 09:20.620
Horubee is very reliable,

09:21.160 --> 09:22.760
so you can count on it.

09:24.130 --> 09:27.530
Why don't we go for a walk together too, Citron?

09:28.480 --> 09:29.040
Good idea.

09:29.570 --> 09:32.940
What's with her?! Just because Mimirol and Horubee have become friends,

09:32.940 --> 09:35.390
it doesn't mean my bro and <i>her</i> should go for a walk too...

09:36.390 --> 09:37.970
I'm so happy for you, Eureka.

09:39.350 --> 09:41.640
Things might work out between those two.

09:44.200 --> 09:46.940
I never should've said "s'il-vous-plaît" to her...

09:48.050 --> 09:51.610
And you know, I got kicked out of my own Gym once!

09:59.900 --> 10:01.490
Lillia-san, are you all right?

10:03.050 --> 10:04.480
Ouch...

10:05.690 --> 10:09.550
Oh my... It was the geeky girl that fell, not Mimirol.

10:09.550 --> 10:10.790
That was a failure.

10:10.790 --> 10:11.930
Plan B, then.

10:13.400 --> 10:14.410
Please hold on.

10:17.890 --> 10:19.400
Thank you very much.

10:22.130 --> 10:23.490
This should do.

10:24.380 --> 10:26.050
Citron, you're so kind.

10:26.380 --> 10:28.060
This is nothing noteworthy.

10:30.280 --> 10:31.070
Lillia-san!

10:33.390 --> 10:34.690
Do you have a moment?

10:35.340 --> 10:35.920
Sure.

10:36.920 --> 10:37.470
This way!

10:41.230 --> 10:42.360
I wonder what the matter is.

10:42.610 --> 10:44.290
Eureka is a good little sister to you.

10:44.690 --> 10:44.930
Huh?

10:45.520 --> 10:46.010
I guess...

10:48.290 --> 10:50.870
Your brother creates all kinds of inventions, huh?

10:51.290 --> 10:54.010
And each and every one of them is amazing!

10:54.510 --> 10:58.090
Each and every one of them is a failure that's bound to explode!

10:59.230 --> 11:01.260
Boom! And your head gets all frizzy.

11:02.490 --> 11:04.200
Failure breeds success.

11:04.790 --> 11:06.850
That's how you get closer and closer to perfecting your work.

11:09.090 --> 11:11.510
My bro may not look that way, but sometimes...

11:11.510 --> 11:13.060
...he wets the bed.

11:13.670 --> 11:15.350
So he has a cute side too!

11:17.160 --> 11:20.230
You know, my bro likes stripping down to his underpants...

11:20.850 --> 11:24.150
...and having an Arbok wrap itself around his entire body.

11:25.260 --> 11:26.800
That's lovely!

11:26.800 --> 11:28.910
An Arbok's skin is really nice to the touch, after all!

11:32.240 --> 11:33.450
This won't work...

11:36.720 --> 11:37.680
Pokémon Quiz.

11:38.070 --> 11:39.000
The answer is...?

11:40.950 --> 11:50.830
Coming up next:

11:40.950 --> 11:45.920
The evil clutches of the Rocket Gang!

11:41.870 --> 11:46.550
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:45.920 --> 11:50.830
Eureka is in big trouble!!

11:59.840 --> 12:00.940
All right, wanna go?

12:02.530 --> 12:05.720
Can I accompany you to the next Pokémon Center?

12:05.720 --> 12:06.820
Yeah, let's go!

12:07.160 --> 12:07.740
Please do!

12:14.460 --> 12:15.830
Is your leg okay?

12:16.140 --> 12:17.820
Yeah, I'm completely fine now.

12:18.080 --> 12:19.290
I'm not even tired any more!

12:20.200 --> 12:21.690
Bro, let's hold hands!

12:21.930 --> 12:25.000
Hey, Eureka! What is with you all of a sudden?

12:25.000 --> 12:25.930
Just do it!

12:31.960 --> 12:32.490
Ow...

12:39.890 --> 12:40.700
What's this?!

12:42.850 --> 12:45.110
If you say "What's this?! Pika!",

12:45.510 --> 12:47.360
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

12:48.130 --> 12:49.870
To prevent the world's destruction!

12:50.430 --> 12:52.600
To protect the world's peace!

12:52.990 --> 12:55.560
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

12:55.850 --> 12:58.370
we're lovely, charmy villains!

12:59.330 --> 13:00.140
Musashi!

13:00.600 --> 13:00.920
Kojiro!

13:01.510 --> 13:04.400
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

13:04.640 --> 13:07.650
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

13:07.650 --> 13:09.100
Just kidding!

13:11.470 --> 13:12.970
Charm!

13:13.610 --> 13:14.380
Rocket Gang!

13:14.830 --> 13:16.690
Give back Horubee and Mimirol!

13:17.160 --> 13:17.600
Who are they?

13:17.910 --> 13:20.430
They're bad guys who steal Pokémon from others!

13:21.610 --> 13:21.990
What?!

13:28.750 --> 13:32.130
We're taking this cute and floofy Mimirol!

13:32.380 --> 13:34.190
Bye!

13:37.030 --> 13:38.990
Are you all right, Yancham, Harimaron?

13:40.210 --> 13:41.760
Bro!

13:42.040 --> 13:42.700
Lillia-san!

13:45.720 --> 13:46.910
Aw, geez!

13:47.660 --> 13:48.670
Mimirol...

13:48.950 --> 13:52.810
I will get back Horubee and your Mimirol for sure, Lillia-san!

13:53.090 --> 13:53.470
Okay.

13:54.360 --> 13:57.310
Now is the time for science to open up the future!

13:58.010 --> 13:59.520
Citronic Gear, on!

14:00.170 --> 14:02.970
For times like this, I have prepared a nice machine!

14:03.420 --> 14:05.030
It is called "Observe the Progress of Protection"!

14:05.410 --> 14:06.700
Wow!

14:06.700 --> 14:11.870
The band-aids I put on Lillia-san and Horubee earlier had tracking devices integrated in them,

14:12.350 --> 14:13.840
so if we use this machine... Look...

14:14.680 --> 14:16.240
Oh, it's reacting.

14:17.670 --> 14:19.590
Technology is incredible!

14:19.850 --> 14:20.880
Let us use it right away...

14:25.610 --> 14:26.750
It has discovered them!

14:27.100 --> 14:28.650
All right, lead the way!

14:29.240 --> 14:29.830
This way!

14:38.690 --> 14:41.100
Hehe, we got Mimirol!

14:41.330 --> 14:43.020
We got our charm!

14:44.090 --> 14:45.400
Mimirol! Horubee!

14:45.400 --> 14:45.860
Gulp!

14:46.670 --> 14:48.010
How did you find us?

14:48.010 --> 14:49.530
My brother's invention helped us!

14:50.210 --> 14:51.870
Come on out, Pumpjin!

14:52.250 --> 14:53.640
You too, Maaiika!

14:55.740 --> 14:56.650
Shadow Ball!

14:59.660 --> 15:01.050
Harimaron, Pin Missile!

15:05.410 --> 15:06.930
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

15:09.810 --> 15:10.800
Psybeam!

15:13.570 --> 15:15.050
Rentorar, please come out!

15:17.400 --> 15:18.430
Thunder Fang!

15:23.270 --> 15:25.070
Use Psybeam once more!

15:25.070 --> 15:25.940
Shadow Ball!

15:27.150 --> 15:27.940
Dodge!

15:33.690 --> 15:34.790
Eureka!

15:37.640 --> 15:38.990
Eureka!

15:42.190 --> 15:42.890
Bro!

15:43.410 --> 15:44.480
It will be fine!

15:44.830 --> 15:45.290
Okay.

15:45.640 --> 15:46.830
Shadow Ball!

15:48.550 --> 15:49.180
Dodge!

15:50.750 --> 15:52.530
Yancham, we'll go too!

15:52.870 --> 15:53.990
Stone Edge!

15:57.490 --> 15:58.270
Seed Bomb!

16:01.790 --> 16:04.010
Eureka, please do not move!

16:04.450 --> 16:06.010
I will pull you up now!

16:06.010 --> 16:06.780
Will you be all right?

16:07.870 --> 16:08.400
We will!

16:12.920 --> 16:14.280
Bro!

16:14.280 --> 16:15.090
It will be fine.

16:15.390 --> 16:17.650
Believe in me and my device!

16:19.440 --> 16:19.660
Okay!

16:33.330 --> 16:33.920
Look.

16:34.410 --> 16:35.400
Everything is fine now.

16:36.920 --> 16:37.830
Bro...

16:37.830 --> 16:38.800
Thank goodness.

16:41.770 --> 16:42.750
Your turn, Tairenar!

16:43.170 --> 16:44.030
Fire Blast!

16:49.440 --> 16:50.650
Pikachu, Electro Ball!

16:55.270 --> 16:56.150
Are you hurt?

16:56.570 --> 16:57.860
No, I'm fine.

16:58.780 --> 17:00.460
But your Eipam Arm...

17:01.210 --> 17:03.540
It is nothing. I can repair it in no time!

17:04.770 --> 17:07.800
What is most important is that I was able to protect you, Eureka.

17:09.390 --> 17:10.250
Bro...

17:20.930 --> 17:23.870
We won't hand this charm over, no matter what!

17:25.680 --> 17:28.290
Pikachu, use Iron Tail to cut that net!

17:35.500 --> 17:36.170
Guys!

17:36.620 --> 17:37.820
Thank goodness, Mimirol!

17:40.070 --> 17:40.660
All right.

17:41.190 --> 17:41.440
Huh?

17:41.760 --> 17:42.820
I have a bad feeling about this.

17:43.080 --> 17:44.630
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

17:52.640 --> 17:58.860
I would've really liked to have that cute and sweet Mimirol so it could enhance my mature sex appeal.

17:59.650 --> 18:02.860
I would've liked for the Rocket Gang to have some charm.

18:02.860 --> 18:05.000
I have Maaiika with me, so it's fine.

18:06.170 --> 18:08.610
This feels bad!

18:11.630 --> 18:12.320
Mimirol!

18:12.800 --> 18:13.750
Are you all right?

18:15.360 --> 18:17.090
I am glad it is safe.

18:17.530 --> 18:19.900
Thank you, Citron, guys.

18:20.270 --> 18:20.800
It was nothing.

18:25.550 --> 18:26.110
All right,

18:26.690 --> 18:27.870
I'm leaving now.

18:28.280 --> 18:28.550
Huh?

18:29.030 --> 18:31.620
Didn't you say you'd accompany us to the next Pokémon Center...?

18:32.240 --> 18:32.880
I won't.

18:33.570 --> 18:39.130
I realized that, as someone who's looking for a partner, I need to improve myself a lot more.

18:40.040 --> 18:42.800
It seems like I'm still lacking appeal.

18:51.110 --> 18:53.400
Eureka, make sure to get along with your brother.

18:54.470 --> 18:54.880
Sure!

18:56.950 --> 18:58.270
Mimirol, let's go!

19:04.480 --> 19:05.970
Lillia-san, take care.

19:08.280 --> 19:09.590
Let's meet again!

19:09.930 --> 19:11.370
Bye-bye!

19:14.960 --> 19:16.480
Take care!

19:17.890 --> 19:20.400
I'm glad you're my bro, bro.

19:21.910 --> 19:23.170
What? What do you mean?

19:24.840 --> 19:26.070
Nothing.

19:28.940 --> 19:30.870
Citron has saved his little sister from danger...

19:31.740 --> 19:34.990
...and Eureka has once again felt the strength of the bond with her brother.

19:35.970 --> 19:39.960
And so, Satoshi and his friends continue their journey.

19:46.640 --> 19:47.500
Let me see...

19:47.810 --> 19:48.950
How is this?

19:49.350 --> 19:50.300
Is it repaired?

19:50.630 --> 19:51.500
It is perfect!

19:55.800 --> 19:57.210
Bro, what's this?

20:06.240 --> 20:06.770
Cough.

20:08.300 --> 20:12.560
I guess I <i>do</i> have to look for a reliable wife for you, after all...

20:13.800 --> 20:15.130
Young lady, let me keep you!

20:15.480 --> 20:17.680
Please have my brother, s'il-vous-plaît!

20:18.280 --> 20:18.960
Huh?

20:18.960 --> 20:19.980
Eureka!

20:20.550 --> 20:25.240
I told you to stop doing that!

20:28.920 --> 20:30.580
PokéLove TV!

20:31.200 --> 20:35.400
All right, here comes PokéLove TV, which spreads the charm of Pokémon to the world!

20:35.400 --> 20:36.470
The hosts are I, Ken, and...

20:36.470 --> 20:38.300
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:38.300 --> 20:40.310
Today we will introduce Dedenne!

20:40.310 --> 20:42.810
Oh my, it's round cheeks are so cute!

20:42.810 --> 20:45.510
Uh-oh... Those cute cheeks contains paralyzing electricity!

20:45.790 --> 20:49.920
Dedenne is a powerful Pokémon who stores more electricity in its cheek pouches than its looks would have you imagine,

20:49.920 --> 20:52.860
then uses it to paralyze its opponents.

20:52.860 --> 20:54.850
Wow, Dedenne is amazing!

20:55.100 --> 20:56.280
All right, I've decided!

20:56.280 --> 20:57.190
What?

20:57.190 --> 21:00.400
I was thinking of catching lots of Dedenne and saving electricity costs.

21:00.400 --> 21:02.800
You can't save costs with Dedenne, no!

21:08.090 --> 21:08.800
Look!

21:09.630 --> 21:10.700
It's amazing!

21:15.150 --> 21:16.200
Why?!

21:16.720 --> 21:18.300
Oh, they just fell asleep.

21:18.300 --> 21:20.320
Dedenne falls asleep easily, after all.

21:20.860 --> 21:25.820
Sunday April 10th at 8am!

21:21.830 --> 21:24.830
Abareru-kun tries to become a Pokémon movie voice actor!

21:24.540 --> 21:25.510
"Believe in yourself"

21:28.110 --> 21:30.010
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.210 --> 21:31.390
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.320 --> 21:33.430
Rock 'n' roll!

21:33.640 --> 21:35.510
I'm Jimmy, the Pikachu Trainer!

21:35.930 --> 21:38.560
Satoshi from Masara Town, you're rumored to be super strong!

21:38.840 --> 21:40.770
I want to fight your Pikachu!

21:40.960 --> 21:43.650
Uh, right now Satoshi can't bat-

21:43.650 --> 21:45.200
Rock 'n' roll!

21:45.680 --> 21:48.150
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:48.610 --> 21:51.790
Serena Becomes Satoshi! The Ultimate Pikachu Showdown!!

21:52.360 --> 21:55.810
Next Time

21:52.360 --> 21:55.810
Serena Becomes Satoshi!
The Ultimate Pikachu Showdown!!

21:52.760 --> 21:54.600
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:55.850 --> 22:05.820
